\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0   Golgotha in spirit see,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Christ our Lord, His life there off'ring;
\par Heart and mind be stirr'd then be;
\par Oh, repent, soul, see His suffering!
\par Hard as stone your heart would be
\par If you lacked in sympathy,
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Lamb of God, Thou bears our shame,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Pains and death for us hast suff'red
\par Thou has taken all, the blame,
\par Thro' it love and grace has off'red.
\par That we may not suffer loss,
\par Thou didst die upon the cross.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. One thing I make known to Thee,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  my heart will  be dedicated
\par  unto Thee and ever be
\par  closer to Thy cross related.
\par  Thou art mine and I with Thee
\par  Living, suff'ring dying be.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Help me, Lord, my faith maintain
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Overcoming all temptations
\par  At the cross I would remain,
\par  waiting Thine in love and patience.
\par  At the cross all fears are still'd
\par \pard      With the words; "it is fulfilled"\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

